{"title":"2023 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 2023 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all composite integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> that satisfy the following property: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b935808e571b8054beca04324e72b7d39c53a00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1,d_2,\\dots,d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> are all the positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e5f12a74bd69e4381fcf44aa1d37f1c1f17e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_1&lt;d_2&lt;\\dots&lt;d_k=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7775e33f3677b0b131dcd51dfd58106aa1829825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{i+1}+d_{i+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1e6ddfc11e72523c0cdc09c5bcd49fa3497388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i \\le k-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd9a79b499a99a34e164f71a92b0727f50109c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b9df54f6ae469b584cd80f26d39255ffc7041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43a2070858da2305a10781e5249b1ea7639a7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E \\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. The line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Denote the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/74577a535149ffa62098ac21eed6bec76b5f8393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c30f9fb9f513cc02b19541e52803ebfc829760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\neq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that the line tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> meets line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b9df54f6ae469b584cd80f26d39255ffc7041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> on the internal angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87c2b4566d22220a6ba3b51d206a466e07ef257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geqslant 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, determine all infinite sequences of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56551a1cd4be3a5d996736e858917416035f3c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> for which there exists a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f06f0c47c3a3ca538f1b16ab264179ef7d8e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=x^k+c_{k-1} x^{k-1}+\\cdots+c_1 x+c_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"22\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d79fb1bd20571ade92582af5fc9f1d8e63a083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_0, c_1, \\ldots, c_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" /> are non-negative integers, such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e9095fe41091db78cfab1b7c22211df21037aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P\\left(a_n\\right)=a_{n+1} a_{n+2} \\cdots a_{n+k}\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" />\nfor every integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd637ab33d51cf34fea5d81ba8317243a24b74b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geqslant 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/1196f6f2c31589964db8256cd62edc28a0e807ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\cdots , x_{2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" /> be pairwise different positive real numbers such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25fd754290b76c3cb6ee24ce96d6e2127e0fee31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = \\sqrt{(x_1+x_2+ \\text{···} +x_n)(\\frac1{x_1} + \\frac1{x_2} + \\text{···} +\\frac1{x_n})}\\]\" width=\"371\" height=\"43\" />\nis an integer for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f158f25a00a49541cdbb00e1b60a18573fbe41da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1,2,\\cdots,2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/68830fec75b013c8299ee38c1df4373082f03eeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2023} \\ge 3034$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. A Japanese triangle consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314149be9582842c3e8efe75b62a4f32fc1d3463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\dots + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" /> circles arranged in an equilateral triangular shape such that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7746ed746b280e2a83d7defebe5cfe5d557fc9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbd55597272a9914166c5dd1e71a5d23d842ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{th}$\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> row contains exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> circles, exactly one of which is coloured red. A ninja path in a Japanese triangle is a sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> circles obtained by starting in the top row, then repeatedly going from a circle to one of the two circles immediately below it and finishing in the bottom row. Here is an example of a Japanese triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, along with a ninja path in that triangle containing two red circles.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba6b5fd48bca54a3103c12a3fd27b464a32abf2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // credit to vEnhance for the diagram (which was better than my original asy): size(4cm);   pair X = dir(240); pair Y = dir(0);   path c = scale(0.5)*unitcircle;   int[] t = {0,0,2,2,3,0};   for (int i=0; i&lt;=5; ++i) {     for (int j=0; j&lt;=i; ++j) {       filldraw(shift(i*X+j*Y)*c, (t[i]==j) ? lightred : white);       draw(shift(i*X+j*Y)*c);     }   }   draw((0,0)--(X+Y)--(2*X+Y)--(3*X+2*Y)--(4*X+2*Y)--(5*X+2*Y),linewidth(1.5));   path q = (3,-3sqrt(3))--(-3,-3sqrt(3));   draw(q,Arrows(TeXHead, 1));   label(&quot;$n = 6$&quot;, q, S); label(&quot;$n = 6$&quot;, q, S); [/asy]\" width=\"178\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p>In terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, find the greatest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that in each Japanese triangle there is a ninja path containing at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> red circles.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an equilateral triangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a7c6b51961d859489bdf038ec21f2c17720c448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,B_1,C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> be interior points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e33b82e3a34f8d17008c8166eaff883d88f4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA_1=A_1C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546a8e1ea8168d325dd5c8e3f4012f35ef22822b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB_1=B_1A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51b650123bc86eee619a5b1f156cc30761172ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC_1=C_1B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/16178c056d256d3702ee4b501044e9de5f4e9e5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BA_1C+\\angle CB_1A+\\angle AC_1B=480^\\circ\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"16\" />Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168608dcef0e370f34a7b4755c6bb4ffe626c0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0eb9f53dc0630afe55b17cdbd6918b547dc0493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359df21188dbd267292a1b07c5ca34045b854d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c54ccfa77b69efc23e15d107177d0bb82563ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a454e0fb01c13d269cb4c9c46d60c2a796ab39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2659f60da1bafdbc157beed4f121d74f4ca936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e472e2e26b1e6ca0f2ae9363136b3c1f675aaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/617653db67675f75d05ef9764c7971c839109cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b97f75ff19cf530ab5d58805c081503fb6b0e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Prove that if triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1815ca31a0a4b18b725b690862a84de67aed84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_1C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> is scalene, then the three circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87af03bb7a880d98421f615310606d80c6972b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA_1A_2, BB_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0361cf89188d03e7f57f204f45083e411540e97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC_1C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> all pass through two common points.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO\" title=\"2023 IMO\">2023 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO\" title=\"2023 IMO\">2023 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_IMO\" title=\"2022 IMO\">2022 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Probl